---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Retry storm in a call chain" hint="A calls B calls ... calls C. C goes bad for 20 seconds and is then fixed. Every hop has a mesh proxy that retries. Change the retry, timeout and breaker settings and see how many requests C receives and whether the chain recovers.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Start with the default (<b>C slow</b>, <b>3 immediate retries</b> at every hop, <b>250 ms timeout</b>, 4 services). Retries multiply across the 3 hops, so C receives up to <b>64 times</b> the user traffic (<b>32,000 per second</b>) while it can serve 375. After second 30 C is fixed, but its queue is full of requests whose callers gave up, so the chain <b>stays broken</b>: a retry storm.</li>
    <li>Choose <b>3 with backoff and a retry budget</b>: the extra load is capped at about <b>1.7 times</b> the user traffic, and the chain is healthy <b>1 second</b> after the fix.</li>
    <li>Go back to immediate retries and turn on the <b>circuit breaker</b>: after one bad second the proxy stops sending C anything but a few probes, the queue drains, and the chain recovers 1 second after the fix. Then turn the breaker off and raise the depth to <b>6</b>: immediate retries multiply by 4 at each of 5 hops, which is 1,024 times the user traffic (512,000 per second).</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg smb" data-smb>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Services in the chain <select class="pg-in" data-depth>
        <option value="2">2 (A calls C)</option>
        <option value="3">3 (A, B, C)</option>
        <option value="4" selected>4 (A, B, D, C)</option>
        <option value="5">5</option>
        <option value="6">6</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>What is wrong with C <select class="pg-in" data-fault>
        <option value="slow" selected>C is 4 times slower (serves 375 per second)</option>
        <option value="err">C fails 30% of calls (some bad pods)</option>
        <option value="down">C is down (every call fails fast)</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Retries at every hop <select class="pg-in" data-retry>
        <option value="none">none</option>
        <option value="imm" selected>3 immediate retries</option>
        <option value="budget">3 with backoff and a retry budget</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Timeout at every hop <select class="pg-in" data-timeout>
        <option value="none">none (30 s)</option>
        <option value="t250" selected>250 ms per try</option>
        <option value="t1000">1 s per try</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Proxy <select class="pg-in" data-proxy>
        <option value="lib">library in the app (0.1 ms per hop)</option>
        <option value="ambient">per-node proxy + waypoint (0.7 ms per hop)</option>
        <option value="sidecar" selected>sidecar proxies (1.0 ms per hop)</option>
      </select></label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" data-brk /> Circuit breaker / outlier ejection on C</label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Requests hitting C</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Success seen by users</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Latency of a successful request</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Added by the proxies</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-box" data-b5>
      <h3>Attempts per second reaching C (log scale)</h3>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 240 84" role="img" aria-label="Attempts per second reaching C over 60 seconds on a log scale, with the fault between seconds 10 and 30 and a dashed line for C's capacity" style="width:100%;height:auto;max-height:190px">
        <rect x="40" y="0" width="40" height="70" style="fill:var(--bad);opacity:.12"></rect>
        <g data-grid></g>
        <polyline data-cap fill="none" style="stroke:var(--muted);stroke-width:1;stroke-dasharray:3 2" points=""></polyline>
        <polyline data-load fill="none" style="stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:1.6" points=""></polyline>
        <text x="2" y="81" style="fill:var(--muted);font-size:6px">0 s</text>
        <text x="40" y="81" style="fill:var(--muted);font-size:6px">fault 10 s</text>
        <text x="82" y="81" style="fill:var(--muted);font-size:6px">fixed at 30 s</text>
        <text x="222" y="81" style="fill:var(--muted);font-size:6px">60 s</text>
      </svg>
      <span class="pg-note">Dashed line: what C can serve. The shaded band is the fault.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-box" data-b6>
      <h3>Success rate seen by users</h3>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 240 60" role="img" aria-label="Share of user requests that succeed over 60 seconds, with the fault between seconds 10 and 30" style="width:100%;height:auto;max-height:150px">
        <rect x="40" y="0" width="40" height="50" style="fill:var(--bad);opacity:.12"></rect>
        <line x1="0" y1="50" x2="240" y2="50" style="stroke:var(--muted);stroke-width:.5"></line>
        <line x1="0" y1="2" x2="240" y2="2" style="stroke:var(--muted);stroke-width:.3;stroke-dasharray:2 2"></line>
        <g data-open></g>
        <polyline data-succ fill="none" style="stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:1.6" points=""></polyline>
        <text x="2" y="58" style="fill:var(--muted);font-size:6px">0%</text>
        <text x="220" y="9" style="fill:var(--muted);font-size:6px">100%</text>
      </svg>
      <span class="pg-note">Small bars along the bottom mark the seconds when the breaker is open.</span>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model, in steps of one second: users send 500 requests per second to A. C normally serves 1,500 per second in 20 ms, from a queue of at most 600 requests; when C is slow it serves 375 per second in 80 ms. Each service does 5 ms of its own work, and the proxy cost per hop is the figure in the menu. The same timeout is set on every hop, and a timeout does not cancel the work already sent downstream. Three retries means 4 tries in all. The budget allows retries up to 20% of the requests on a hop, with 25, 50 and 100 ms backoff before each retry. Callers react to the failures of the previous second. The breaker opens when more than half of the attempts to C fail, lets 20 probes per second through, and stays open 2, 4, 8 and then 16 seconds (longer after each repeat); a blocked attempt fails at once and is not retried on that hop. Times are means, so the numbers are approximate.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-smb]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement | SVGElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    const L = 500, MU = 1500, QMAX = 600, TICKS = 60, F0 = 10, F1 = 30, PROBES = 20, SVC = 20, OWN = 5, BUDGET = 0.2;
    const BACKOFF = [25, 50, 100];
    const PROXY: Record<string, number> = { lib: 0.1, ambient: 0.7, sidecar: 1.0 };
    const TIMEOUT: Record<string, number> = { none: 30000, t250: 250, t1000: 1000 };
    const clamp = (x: number, a: number, b: number) => Math.max(a, Math.min(b, x));
    type Att = { s: number; dOK: number; dF: number; nr?: number };
    type St = { ok: number; to: number; err: number; rej: number; dOK: number; block: number };
    type Cfg = { depth: number; fault: string; retry: string; timeout: string; breaker: boolean; proxy: string };

    // The outcome of one hop that retries: success probability, number of tries made, mean times.
    function level(att: Att, retry: string) {
      const R = retry === 'none' ? 0 : 3; const f = 1 - att.s; const fr = Math.max(0, f - (att.nr || 0)); let g = 1;
      if (retry === 'budget') {
        const extra = (x: number) => { let sum = 0, p = 1; for (let k = 1; k <= R; k++) { p *= x * fr; sum += p; } return sum; };
        if (extra(1) > BUDGET) { let lo = 0, hi = 1; for (let i = 0; i < 40; i++) { const m = (lo + hi) / 2; if (extra(m) > BUDGET) hi = m; else lo = m; } g = lo; }
      }
      const back = (k: number) => (retry === 'budget' ? BACKOFF[Math.min(k, 2)] : 0);
      let S = 0, tries = 0, tSucc = 0, tFail = 0, pFail = 0, reach = 1, delay = 0;
      for (let k = 0; k <= R; k++) {
        tries += reach; S += reach * att.s; tSucc += reach * att.s * (delay + att.dOK);
        const end = reach * (k === R ? f : f - g * fr); pFail += end; tFail += end * (delay + att.dF);
        reach = reach * fr * (k === R ? 0 : g); delay += att.dF + back(k);
      }
      return { S, tries, dOK: S > 0 ? tSucc / S : att.dOK, dF: pFail > 0 ? tFail / pFail : att.dF };
    }

    function simulate(cfg: Cfg) {
      const H = cfg.depth - 1, T = TIMEOUT[cfg.timeout], pi = PROXY[cfg.proxy];
      let b = 0; let prev: St = { ok: 1, to: 0, err: 0, rej: 0, dOK: SVC, block: 0 };
      let brk = { open: false, since: 0, trips: 0, dur: 2 }; let closedAt = -99;
      const rows: { t: number; load: number; cap: number; success: number; lat: number; amp: number; open: boolean }[] = [];
      const tree = (st: St) => {
        const att0: Att = {
          s: (1 - st.block) * st.ok, nr: st.block, dOK: st.dOK + pi,
          dF: st.block * 0.5 + ((1 - st.block) * (st.to * (T + pi) + st.err * (3 + pi) + st.rej * (1 + pi))) / Math.max(1e-9, st.to + st.err + st.rej),
        };
        let att = att0; const tries: number[] = [];
        for (let h = H; h >= 1; h--) {
          const res = level(att, cfg.retry); tries[h] = res.tries;
          if (h === 1) { att = { s: res.S, dOK: res.dOK + OWN, dF: res.dF + OWN }; break; }
          const dOKn = res.dOK + OWN + pi;
          att = dOKn > T ? { s: 0, dOK: dOKn, dF: T } : { s: res.S, dOK: dOKn, dF: Math.min(T, res.dF + OWN + pi) };
        }
        let total = 1; for (let h = 1; h <= H; h++) total *= tries[h];
        return { total, S: att.s, dOK: att.dOK };
      };
      for (let t = 0; t < TICKS; t++) {
        const inF = t >= F0 && t < F1;
        const mu = cfg.fault === 'slow' && inF ? MU / 4 : MU, svc = cfg.fault === 'slow' && inF ? SVC * 4 : SVC;
        const e = inF ? (cfg.fault === 'err' ? 0.3 : cfg.fault === 'down' ? 1 : 0) : 0;
        const t1 = tree(prev); const A = L * t1.total; const passed = brk.open ? Math.min(A, PROBES) : A;
        const arr = passed * (1 - e); const acc = Math.min(arr, Math.max(0, QMAX - b + mu)); const rej = arr - acc; const qn = Math.max(0, b + acc - mu);
        const lo = (b / mu) * 1000, hi = (qn / mu) * 1000;
        const fok = hi > lo ? clamp((T - svc - lo) / (hi - lo), 0, 1) : svc + lo <= T ? 1 : 0;
        b = qn; const tot = Math.max(1e-9, passed);
        const st: St = { ok: (acc * fok) / tot, to: (acc * (1 - fok)) / tot, err: (passed * e) / tot, rej: rej / tot, dOK: svc + (lo + hi) / 2, block: A > 0 ? 1 - passed / A : 0 };
        if (cfg.breaker) {
          if (!brk.open && passed >= 20 && 1 - st.ok > 0.5) { const trips = t - closedAt > 10 ? 1 : brk.trips + 1; brk = { open: true, since: t, trips, dur: Math.min(16, 2 * 2 ** (trips - 1)) }; }
          else if (brk.open && t - brk.since >= brk.dur) { if (st.ok >= 0.8) { brk = { ...brk, open: false, since: t }; closedAt = t; st.block = 0; } else brk.since = t; }
        }
        const t2 = tree(st); prev = st;
        rows.push({ t, load: passed, cap: mu, success: t2.S, lat: t2.dOK, amp: t1.total, open: brk.open });
      }
      return rows;
    }

    // Static parts of the charts, built once.
    const NS = 'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';
    const X = (t: number) => (t / (TICKS - 1)) * 240; const LOGMIN = 2, LOGMAX = 6;
    const YL = (v: number) => 70 - ((clamp(Math.log10(Math.max(v, 1)), LOGMIN, LOGMAX) - LOGMIN) / (LOGMAX - LOGMIN)) * 66;
    const grid = q<SVGGElement>('[data-grid]');
    [[1e3, '1k'], [1e4, '10k'], [1e5, '100k'], [1e6, '1M']].forEach(([v, lab]) => {
      const ln = document.createElementNS(NS, 'line'); ln.setAttribute('x1', '0'); ln.setAttribute('x2', '240'); ln.setAttribute('y1', String(YL(v as number))); ln.setAttribute('y2', String(YL(v as number)));
      ln.setAttribute('style', 'stroke:var(--muted);stroke-width:.3;stroke-dasharray:1 3'); grid.append(ln);
      const tx = document.createElementNS(NS, 'text'); tx.setAttribute('x', '2'); tx.setAttribute('y', String(YL(v as number) - 1.5)); tx.setAttribute('style', 'fill:var(--muted);font-size:6px'); tx.textContent = String(lab); grid.append(tx);
    });
    const openG = q<SVGGElement>('[data-open]');
    const bars: SVGRectElement[] = Array.from({ length: TICKS }, (_, t) => {
      const r = document.createElementNS(NS, 'rect'); r.setAttribute('x', String(X(t) - 1.5)); r.setAttribute('width', '3'); r.setAttribute('y', '46'); r.setAttribute('height', '4'); r.setAttribute('style', 'fill:var(--accent)'); r.setAttribute('visibility', 'hidden'); openG.append(r); return r;
    });

    const fmt = (n: number) => Math.round(n).toLocaleString('en-US');
    const pct = (x: number) => `${Math.round(x * 100)}%`;
    function draw() {
      const cfg: Cfg = { depth: Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-depth]').value), fault: q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-fault]').value, retry: q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-retry]').value, timeout: q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-timeout]').value, breaker: q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-brk]').checked, proxy: q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-proxy]').value };
      const rows = simulate(cfg); const H = cfg.depth - 1;
      const during = rows.filter((r) => r.t >= F0 && r.t < F1), after = rows.filter((r) => r.t >= 40);
      const avg = (a: typeof rows, f: (r: (typeof rows)[0]) => number) => a.reduce((x, r) => x + f(r), 0) / a.length;
      const succDuring = avg(during, (r) => r.success), succAfter = avg(after, (r) => r.success);
      const total = during.reduce((x, r) => x + r.load, 0), peak = Math.max(...rows.map((r) => r.load));
      let rec = -1; for (let t = F1; t < TICKS; t++) if (rows.slice(t).every((r) => r.success >= 0.95)) { rec = t - F1; break; }
      const okRows = during.filter((r) => r.success > 0.01); const latDuring = okRows.length ? avg(okRows, (r) => r.lat) : -1;
      const base = rows[5].lat; const hopMs = PROXY[cfg.proxy] * H;
      const amp = total / (L * (F1 - F0));
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = `peak ${fmt(peak)} per second`;
      q('[data-n1]').textContent = `${fmt(total)} in the 20 s fault, ${amp.toFixed(1)} times the ${fmt(L * (F1 - F0))} the users sent; C can serve ${fmt(MU / (cfg.fault === 'slow' ? 4 : 1))} per second`;
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = `${pct(succDuring)} during the fault, ${pct(succAfter)} after`;
      q('[data-n2]').textContent = rec === 0 ? 'healthy again as soon as C was fixed' : rec > 0 ? `healthy again ${rec} s after the fix` : 'never recovers by itself';
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = `${Math.round(base)} ms healthy, ${latDuring < 0 ? 'no successes' : `${fmt(latDuring)} ms in the fault`}`;
      q('[data-n3]').textContent = latDuring < 0 ? 'every request failed during the fault' : `about ${fmt((L * latDuring) / 1000)} requests in flight at A during the fault, against ${fmt((L * base) / 1000)} when healthy`;
      q('[data-o4]').textContent = `${hopMs.toFixed(1)} ms of ${Math.round(base)} ms (${Math.round((hopMs / base) * 100)}%)`;
      q('[data-n4]').textContent = `${H} hop${H > 1 ? 's' : ''} at ${PROXY[cfg.proxy].toFixed(1)} ms; the worst case is a retry storm, not the proxy`;
      q<SVGPolylineElement>('[data-load]').setAttribute('points', rows.map((r) => `${X(r.t).toFixed(1)},${YL(r.load).toFixed(1)}`).join(' '));
      q<SVGPolylineElement>('[data-cap]').setAttribute('points', rows.map((r) => `${X(r.t).toFixed(1)},${YL(r.cap).toFixed(1)}`).join(' '));
      q<SVGPolylineElement>('[data-succ]').setAttribute('points', rows.map((r) => `${X(r.t).toFixed(1)},${(50 - r.success * 48).toFixed(1)}`).join(' '));
      rows.forEach((r, i) => bars[i].setAttribute('visibility', r.open ? 'visible' : 'hidden'));
      const stuck = succAfter < 0.5; const storm = amp >= 5;
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b1]').style.setProperty('--c', storm ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b2]').style.setProperty('--c', stuck ? 'var(--bad)' : succDuring > 0.9 ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--accent)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b3]').style.setProperty('--c', 'var(--accent)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b4]').style.setProperty('--c', 'var(--accent)');
      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); out.classList.toggle('bad', stuck);
      out.textContent = stuck ? `Retry storm. Each try fails, so each hop sends ${cfg.retry === 'imm' ? '4' : 'several'} tries and the multiplication over ${H} hop${H > 1 ? 's' : ''} sends C up to ${fmt(peak)} attempts per second. After the fix at second 30 its queue is still full of requests the callers have given up on, so nothing succeeds: the chain stays down until the traffic is cut off.`
        : storm ? `A storm formed (${amp.toFixed(1)} times the user traffic reached C), but it ended ${rec > 0 ? `${rec} s` : 'at once'} after the fix. ${cfg.timeout === 'none' ? 'With no timeout the callers wait instead of retrying, so users see slow responses rather than errors.' : 'A longer timeout or a breaker would have kept it smaller.'}`
        : succDuring >= 0.95 ? `Users barely notice: ${pct(succDuring)} of requests succeed during the fault and C receives only ${amp.toFixed(1)} times the user traffic.`
        : `No storm: C received ${amp.toFixed(1)} times the user traffic. ${pct(1 - succDuring)} of user requests failed during the fault${cfg.fault === 'slow' ? (cfg.timeout === 'none' ? ', because C could not serve all of them' : ', because C fell behind and its queue made the replies arrive after the timeout') : cfg.fault === 'down' ? ', because C was down and a retry cannot help' : ''}, and the chain recovered ${rec > 0 ? `${rec} s` : 'at once'} after the fix.`;
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw); root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
